{"name":"Icelandish","hex":"#ccdfdc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Icelandish","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Icelandic (North Germanic tongue; Iceland's official language)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Icelandic (of or relating to the North Germanic language spoken in Iceland).","Icelandic (of or relating to the natives or inhabitants of Iceland)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Icelandish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Icelandic language","blocks":[{"text":"Icelandic is a North Germanic language from the Indo-European language family spoken by about 390,000 people, the vast majority of whom live in Iceland, where it is the national language. Since it is a West Scandinavian language, it is most closely related to Faroese, western Norwegian dialects, and the extinct language Norn. It is not mutually intelligible with the continental Scandinavian languages and is more distinct from the most widely spoken Germanic languages, English and German. The written forms of Icelandic and Faroese are very similar, but their spoken forms are not mutually intelligible."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/%C3%8Dslendingas%C3%B6gur.jpg/330px-%C3%8Dslendingas%C3%B6gur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icelandic_language","wikidata":"Q294"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Idioma_island%C3%A9s.PNG/500px-Idioma_island%C3%A9s.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Idioma_island%C3%A9s.PNG/500px-Idioma_island%C3%A9s.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIdioma_island%C3%A9s.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1a/LandnamabokManuscriptPage.jpg?utm_